---
import Shot from './Shot.astro';
import ZoneScene from './ZoneScene.astro';

/**
 * Four short steps. Steps 1 and 4 show real cropped screenshots of the editor and of Settings; steps 2 and 3
 * happen on the desktop, outside Krova's own window, so they are diagrams built from Krova's zone shapes and
 * are labelled as diagrams.
 */
---

<section id="how" class="section" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="sec-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2 id="how-title">Draw once. <span class="soft">Snap from then on.</span></h2>
    </header>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <div class="art">
          <span class="kind">Screenshot</span>
          <div class="crop">
            <Shot
              name="crop-zones"
              alt="The zone editor: three zones on a monitor, the middle one selected, and a dashed guide at 50 percent showing where the next split would go."
            />
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="num">1</p>
        <h3>Draw zones</h3>
        <p>Start from a template or split the screen yourself. Each monitor keeps its own layouts.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <div class="art">
          <span class="kind">Diagram</span>
          <ZoneScene
            state="drag"
            layout="priority"
            target={1}
            label="Diagram: a window is dragged while Shift is held. The three zones of the monitor are shown and the middle one is lit."
          />
        </div>
        <p class="num">2</p>
        <h3>Hold Shift and drag</h3>
        <p>Drag any window and hold Shift, or the key you chose. The zones of the monitor under the cursor appear.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <div class="art">
          <span class="kind">Diagram</span>
          <ZoneScene
            state="snap"
            layout="priority"
            target={1}
            label="Diagram: after release, the window fills the middle zone."
          />
        </div>
        <p class="num">3</p>
        <h3>Release over a zone</h3>
        <p>Let go and the window fills the zone. Release Shift first, or press Esc, and nothing moves.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <div class="art">
          <span class="kind">Screenshot</span>
          <div class="crop">
            <Shot
              name="crop-keyboard"
              alt="Settings, keyboard shortcuts: Ctrl+Alt+Shift with Left moves the focused window to the previous zone, Right to the next, 1 to 9 to that zone number, Up to the next monitor."
            />
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="num">4</p>
        <h3>Or skip the mouse <span class="tag">Windows</span></h3>
        <p>Ctrl+Alt+Shift with Left or Right steps through the zones, 1 to 9 jumps to one.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-l) var(--space-m);
  }

  .step {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .art {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    height: 14.5rem;
    padding: 2rem 1rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
  }
  .art > :global(.scene) {
    max-width: 15.5rem;
  }
  .art .crop {
    --crop-h: 11rem;
  }

  .kind {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.75rem;
    top: 0.65rem;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }


  .num {
    margin-top: var(--space-m);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }
  .step h3 {
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }
  .step h3 + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xs);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 0.3rem;
    padding: 0.05rem 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    vertical-align: 0.1em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
